From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:53:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 22/60] AnalyzerBenchmark: on-device analyzer benchmark

For P5-5 (performance and accelerators). Runs over live frames the caller
captured into memory (never written anywhere; the caller drops them).
For each bundle (the bundled one, then any signed test bundle, verified
against the built-in keys) and each setting (1, 2 and 4 intra-op threads
x CPU, XNNPACK, NNAPI):
- cold preload of a fresh factory (verification and session creation)
  and the accelerator the sessions actually use;
- the first analyze() of a new analyzer, 10 warm-up calls, then 3 timed
  passes with per-stage p50/p95 (detect, mesh, pad, cues, quality, pose,
  total; a stage counts on the frames where it ran);
- parity on a fresh analyzer against the reference (first bundle, CPU,
  1 thread): max |delta livenessScore|, max landmark distance in px and
  frames where only one side has a score or landmarks. A setting matches
  at <= 0.01, <= 0.5 px and no mismatch.
report() formats a fixed-width text table (timings and parity only).

Tests: the matrix order, the percentile, landmark flattening, parity
limits and missing scores, and the report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
